{
  "slug": "trapic",
  "name": "Trapic",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Long-term memory for AI coding assistants. Trapic automatically recalls project knowledge at session start, captures decisions and conventions as you work, detects conflicts using\ntopic-based matching, and flags stale knowledge for review. Works via MCP — zero server-side LLM, all intelligence runs on your client AI.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **6 skills**, **1 hook** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (6): `trapic-health` (This skill should be used when the user wants to check knowledge health, see project knowledge statistics, review…), `trapic-knowledge` (This skill should be used when the user is coding, making technical decisions, discovering non-obvious facts, or establishing…), `trapic-pack-from-project` (Package project knowledge into a Trapic marketplace pack), `trapic-pack-quality` (Use when creating marketplace pack content), `trapic-review`, `trapic-search` (Use when the user wants to search project knowledge, find past decisions, look up conventions, or asks \"what…)\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionStart`\n- **MCP servers** (1): `trapic`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install trapic@claude-community` from `nickjazz/trapic-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 6,
    "hook": 1,
    "mcp": 1
  },
